  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Wednesday)\nIssued at 201 PM CDT THU SEP 3 2026\n\nUpper level ridge remains the big story for our weather, helping\npush temperatures up close to 100 degrees in many areas again this\nafternoon. A few showers/storms have also popped up in the heat \nof the afternoon. The big upper ridge is still forecast to break\ndown and shift westward over the next few days, and then \n\"pendulum\" back to the east coast by the middle of next week. \nTemperatures will remain elevated, but confidence in meeting \nadvisory level criteria is lower beyond Saturday. Will therefore \nwait on extending the ongoing Heat Advisory beyond it currently \nplanned Saturday expiration. But we may need to either extend it, \nor issue another one next week based. Otherwise, best rain \nchances over the coming days will be in the southern part of the \nCWA, largely due to the presence of a tropical wave along the Gulf\ncoast. \n\n/61/",
